Let the whistle have natural frequency \(
u_0\) and let the source train move with speed \(u\). For the stationary detector, the **Doppler effect** gives \(
u_1 = 
u_0  rac{v_{sound}}{v_{sound} - u}\) (the source factor would have a plus sign if it were receding; it cancels either way).

The listener in the second train moves towards the source with speed \(v\), so the listener factor changes from \(v_{sound}\) to \(v_{sound} + v\), while the source factor stays the same: \(
u_2 = 
u_0  rac{v_{sound} + v}{v_{sound} - u}\).

Dividing, \( rac{
u_2}{
u_1} =  rac{v_{sound} + v}{v_{sound}} = 1 +  rac{v}{v_{sound}}\). Hence \( rac{v}{v_{sound}} =  rac{
u_2}{
u_1} - 1 =  rac{
u_2 - 
u_1}{
u_1}\).

So the answer is option (D).
